    <h2>What to expect at your first visit</h2>
    <p>Your first visit is mostly about us getting to know you and your mouth. We block out extra time for new patients so nothing feels rushed.</p>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>A real conversation about why you're here and what you'd like out of dental care going forward.</li>
      <li>A comprehensive exam — teeth, gums, bite, and soft-tissue / oral cancer screening.</li>
      <li>Digital X-rays as appropriate (we'll skip them if you've had recent ones we can pull).</li>
      <li>A cleaning, if your gums and time allow at the first visit.</li>
      <li>A clear summary of anything we found and a written treatment plan if work is recommended — no pressure to commit on the spot.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Before your appointment</h2>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li>Bring (or upload ahead of time) your insurance card and a photo ID.</li>
      <li>List any current medications and major medical history.</li>
      <li>Bring a copy of any recent dental X-rays if you've been seen elsewhere in the last 1–2 years.</li>
      <li>If you have anxiety or have had difficult dental experiences before, tell us when you book — we'll plan accordingly.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Insurance &amp; payment</h2>
    <p>We work with most major PPO dental plans. We don't yet directly bill HMO/DMO plans. For procedures your insurance doesn't fully cover, we offer Cherry, CareCredit, and in-house payment options. See our <a href="/insurance-financing/">insurance &amp; financing page</a> for details.</p>

    <h2>Patient forms</h2>
    <p>To save time on the day of your visit, we'll email you a secure new-patient intake form when you book. Please fill it out before you arrive.</p>
